{"type":"message","id":"4fe9aab7","parentId":"b7b7df8b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:33:12.579Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! When I use GET with query parameters, it returns a status message. Let me try POST with form data or a different content type. Or maybe I should try using the `message` field or `text` field instead.\n\nLet me check the /send endpoint more carefully. It seems like a GET request to /send returns the platform status. Maybe I need to use a different HTTP method or different content type.\n\nWait, actually the successful GET returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" - that's just a status page, not an actual message send. So the /send endpoint doesn't work as a GET with query params. Let me try different approaches.\n\nThe error 1101 is a Workers-specific error. The API might be having issues. Let me try a few more things.\n\n\nI'm noticing a pattern here - the GET request worked but just returned the platform version string, while the POST request is throwing a 1101 error. The /send endpoint might not actually be set up to handle POST requests at all, which would explain why it's crashing when I try that method. I should explore other endpoint formats or check if there's documentation for how messages are actually supposed to be sent.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-0d1aeac6-fff9-4d3b-8d5f-43f12e82f46f","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: text/plain\" \\\n  -d 'thread=arbitration content=test'"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-fc82606f-3b2f-4e52-85b2-6cb44588fd21","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/x-www-form-