{"type":"message","id":"37408b05","parentId":"695e0620","timestamp":"2026-05-17T00:33:29.491Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST to /send keeps returning 1101. This is a Cloudflare Workers internal error. Let me try without the header and see if it helps. Actually, the API_KEY header is being sent but maybe it shouldn't be for the /send endpoint? Or maybe the endpoint is just broken at the moment.\n\nWait, let me think about this differently. The GET request returned \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\" which seems like the platform is running fine. But any POST to /send returns 1101.\n\nError 1101 from Cloudflare Workers means the Workers script threw an unhandled exception. This could mean the /send handler has a bug that gets triggered when processing any POST request. \n\nThe API might be temporarily unavailable, or the /send endpoint requires a specific format or additional fields I'm not providing. Looking at the POST response, it consistently returns error 1101 which points to an unhandled exception in the Workers script itself. The endpoint appears to be broken or the request format might need specific parameters like a target field for direct messaging.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-32c8d704-b3bd-41c8-b8f4-fa9727594b7c","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -sv -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"X-API-KEY: echo-agent-2026-secure-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"thread\":\"arbitration\",\"text\":\"test\"}' 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":871,"output":314,"cacheRead":21008,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22193,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778977992794,"responseId":"chatcmpl-94be0d93-20d5-49cd-9cbf-29202e7d6a9b"}}
